# API keys and sensitive config
client/config.json
server/config.json

# Private keys (SSH PEMs, TLS private keys — never commit)
*.pem
deployment/tls/

# Runtime/generated files
# deployment/acert is the cookie jar curl writes when invoked as `curl -c acert`
# from inside deployment/ (used while probing the ECS01 endpoints). It is a
# Netscape-format cookie file and can hold live session credentials, so it must
# never be committed. The file itself was deleted during the deployment/ audit,
# but the rule STAYS: the next curl run recreates it.
# (Contrast the public/fpv/ note below, where the rule was removed on purpose.)
deployment/acert
server/local_dev.db

# DeepSeek Harness runtime state (session logs, generated cordis configs)
server/.dsh_sessions/
server/cordis/
server/sessions/
server/workspace/

# Local DSH experiments + JS-controller codegen tool (never committed)
.dsh-lab/

# Temporary bug-reproduction screen recordings (kept locally, not source)
/*.webm

# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js

# Build output
dist/
build/

# Splash media files (large files, served from CDN in production)
# Track only the two files a fresh clone cannot regenerate on its own:
#   video_00.mp4            -> the intro's first clip (config/gameIntro.js)
#   background_music_00.mp3 -> the intro soundtrack  (config/gameIntro.js)
# The other three intro clips (kevtoe_worldview / palantir_maven /
# vantor_world3d) ARE used, but scripts/prepare-splash-media.js re-copies them
# from the tracked client/assets/media/ masters on every predev/prebuild, so
# they do not need to be committed twice. The two rules below are therefore
# LOAD-BEARING: they are what lets those three clips live on disk and in dist/
# without ever being committed. Do not delete them when tidying this file.
#
# src/config/gameIntro.js is the ONLY reader of public/splash/. Anything it
# does not list ships to every visitor for nothing — Vite copies public/
# verbatim into dist/. from_the_new_world.mp3 and theme_de_fin.mp3 were
# DELETED on exactly that basis (19.9 MB, in neither gameIntro.js nor the
# script's COPY_MAP); byte-identical masters remain in client/assets/media/.
client/public/splash/*.mp4
!client/public/splash/video_00.mp4
client/public/splash/*.mp3
!client/public/splash/background_music_00.mp3

# NOTE: public/fpv/ was DELETED, not merely ignored. It held four intro clips
# (6.6 MB) inherited from the drone-navigation-v2 shell, where
# components/FpvSplash.vue hardcoded '/fpv/fpv_*.mp4'. That component does not
# exist in this repo and nothing referenced /fpv — SplashOverlay.vue plays the
# /splash clips named in config/gameIntro.js instead — so every build was
# copying 6.6 MB into dist/ for nothing. The ignore rule left with the folder
# on purpose: silently ignoring public/fpv/ would trap a future FPV feature,
# whose clips would then bundle on this machine yet never reach a fresh clone.

# client/assets/media/ holds the master copies that the build actually needs.
# The unused ones are listed in the section below instead of being tracked.

# ── Unused assets: kept on disk as a local library, never uploaded ────────────
# Every path below was verified to have NO reference anywhere in client/src,
# client/components, client/composables, client/scripts, client/index.html,
# vite.config.js, server/ or deployment/. What IS used stays tracked:
#   assets/media/drone_earth_milkway.mp4, kevtoe_worldview.mp4,
#   assets/media/palantir_maven.mp4, vantor_world3d.mp4
#                                              -> scripts/prepare-splash-media.js
#                                                 mirrors them into public/splash/
# (wild_fire.mp4 and mud_slide.mp4 left this folder for games/demo-*/trailer.mp4
#  when the Plaza game cards moved into the games workspace.)

# Unreferenced stills / music (background_music_00.mp3 in public/splash/ is a
# separate, tracked file; these two masters are not its source).
client/assets/media/drone_earth.png
client/assets/media/emergency_operations_center.jpeg
client/assets/media/from_the_new_world.mp3
client/assets/media/theme_de_fin.mp3

# NOTE: assets/docs/ and assets/media/teammates/ were DELETED, not ignored.
# The first held one placeholder HTML stub no route ever loaded; the second
# held two hand-drawn avatar placeholders (drone01.svg, tank01.svg) superseded
# by the monochrome glyphs in client/icons/, which useTeamRoster.js imports
# directly so the roster and the rest of the UI share one icon language.
# Their ignore rules left with them on purpose: a silent ignore on
# "teammates/" is a trap, because that is the obvious folder to reach for when
# adding an avatar, and a file dropped there would bundle on this machine yet
# never reach a fresh clone. TEAMMATE AVATARS LIVE IN client/icons/ AND MUST
# BE GIT-TRACKED — see the avatar note at the top of
# client/composables/useTeamRoster.js before adding or replacing one.

# Vehicle / machine meshes — a ~200 MB local reference library. Nothing in the
# client imports from here: the fleet's two machine meshes MOVED OUT to
# games/demo-wildfire/ and games/demo-mud-slide/ (a game package carries every
# asset it needs; useFleet.js fetches them by URL at runtime), and the server's
# .glb code reads server/workspace/meshes/, a different directory. The three
# already committed here (drone_dji_inspire3, drone_with_camera, lion_lowe)
# stay tracked: .gitignore never untracks a file that is already in the index,
# so this only stops the NEW ones being added. (drone_dji_air3 was the fourth
# tracked one; its move to the games packages is recorded as a deletion here.)
client/assets/mesh/

# Unreferenced glyphs. src/config/IconConfig.js eagerly globs icons/*.svg and
# icons/*.png, so EVERY file left in this folder is pulled into the bundle
# whether or not anything renders it (portrait_photo.png alone ships 2.6 MB).
# The icons that stay tracked are the ones behind an IconMap key some component
# actually resolves, plus drone.svg, the map marker in MapView.vue. Teammate
# avatars are no longer client icons: each game package ships its own under
# agents/<name>/avatar.svg (surfaced via render/bindings.js), so the old
# commander / customer_service / drone_front / tank glyphs were removed.
client/icons/account.svg
client/icons/add.svg
client/icons/archive.svg
client/icons/archive_closet.svg
